==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{rfe}} The word '''antibiotic''' comes from the Greek words ''anti'', meaning "against", and βίος&nbsp;– ''bios,'' "life," hence "against life."

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌæn.ti.baɪˈɒt.ɪk/|/ˌæn.taɪ.baɪˈɒt.ɪk/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌæn.taɪ.baɪˈɑ.tɪk/|/ˌæn.tə.baɪˈɑ.tɪk/}}
* {{rhymes|ɒtɪk}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{pharmacology}} Any [[substance]] that can [[destroy]] or [[inhibit]] the [[growth]] of [[bacteria]] and similar [[microorganism]]s.

====Hyponyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:antibiotic]]

